+// in place, over its own code and data: a crash about 25 s after start.
+//
+// The layout below is the files' own (worked out from a firmware dump, no data taken from it): magic, version 1, file size,
+// one maximum part size per part type, one alignment per part type, padding, then the part tables. A part whose table entry is
+// all zero does not exist, which the format allows; here no part exists, so Mii heads have no shapes and no textures.
+//   texture file ("NFTR"): 11 part types, tables from 0x160, 318 entries of 28 bytes, data from 0x2428
+//   shape file   ("NFSR"): 12 part types, tables from 0xc4 up to 0x14dd4 (part entries of 88 bytes, then transform tables)
+std::vector<u8> EmptyResource(const char magic[4], u32 part_types, u32 alignment, u32 size) {
