+# kart_runtime: the native engine's own runtime
+
+Engine-independent building blocks for the native engine (kart-recomp `docs/NATIVE_ENGINE.md`). Rules:
+
+- Nothing here includes or names anything from suyu (no `core/`, `common/`, kernel or HLE types). C++20 standard library only
+  (SDL where a component needs a device). It must build and pass its tests on its own: `tests/build_and_run.sh`.
+- The emulator side reaches these through thin adapters in its own files; when the emulator is gone, the adapters go and this stays.
+
+| component | what it is |
+|---|---|
+| `core_scheduler.h` | Host threads sharing virtual CPU cores the way the console's threads do: one running thread per core, strict priority, FIFO among equals, a preemption request for the running thread. Replaces fibers and emulated-core threads. |
+| `direct_memory.h` | The game's address space as one host range read and written in place by the recompiled code, and the fault handler that gives bad pointers the old behaviour: unmapped memory reads as zeros, writes to it are dropped, pages without permission are opened. Linux x86-64. |
